    whyChooseContent: "PlowWow.com has been the Lower Mainland's trusted snow removal partner since 1989. With over 35 years of experience managing winter conditions on Strata properties, we built PlowWow around the three things property managers care about most: predictable pricing (fixed contracts), guaranteed service (5-times booking capacity), and fast response (within 5 hours of any storm). No other Lower Mainland snow removal company offers all three. Our 24/7 operations center, GPS-tracked crews, comprehensive documentation systems, and environmentally responsible practices set us apart from competitors who treat snow removal as a sideline business. For PlowWow, winter maintenance is a core division staffed by dedicated, year-round professionals.",
    industryInsight: "The Lower Mainland snow removal industry is plagued by overbooking. Most companies sign up 50+ properties but only have enough crews to service 10-15 at a time. When a major storm hits, half their clients get left waiting — sometimes for days. PlowWow's 5-times booking model was designed specifically to solve this problem. We schedule five crews for every storm event and maintain a reserve fleet for extreme weather. Combined with our real-time Environment Canada monitoring, GPS dispatch, and pre-positioned equipment, this model delivers the guaranteed 5-hour response that our competitors simply cannot match. The industry is also seeing increasing insurance costs and stricter court interpretations of occupier liability. Properties that once relied on building caretakers are increasingly turning to professional contractors with proper insurance, documented procedures, and commercial equipment — exactly what PlowWow provides.",
    materialsAndMethods: "We maintain an inventory of de-icing materials suited to different conditions and surfaces. Rock salt (sodium chloride) remains our primary product for parking surfaces due to its effectiveness and economy, but we also stock calcium chloride for extreme cold conditions (effective to -30°C), calcium magnesium acetate for environmentally sensitive areas, potassium acetate liquid for pre-treatment applications, and sand for traction on slopes and ramps. Our pre-wetting system applies liquid brine to granular materials before spreading, reducing bounce and scatter while accelerating the melting process. This technology allows us to achieve better results with less material, reducing both cost and environmental impact.",
    strataSpecificContent: "Strata corporations face unique challenges in winter maintenance. Multiple building entrances, shared parking structures, visitor parking areas, playground equipment, and amenity spaces all require attention. Emergency vehicle access must be maintained at all times, and service events must be coordinated with garbage collection schedules, move-in/move-out activities, and resident parking patterns. Our Strata-specific service plans account for all of these factors, and our crew supervisors are trained to communicate proactively with on-site caretakers and property managers. We also provide Strata councils with the documentation they need for AGM reporting, insurance renewals, and bylaw compliance verification.",
    seasonalConsiderations: "The Lower Mainland's winter season typically runs from November through March, although early and late-season events are not uncommon. Our contracts provide coverage from October 15 through April 15 to ensure properties are protected during the entire risk window. Pre-season preparation includes equipment maintenance and testing, crew training and safety briefings, site re-assessment to account for any property changes, and pre-positioning of materials. Post-season activities include equipment inspection and storage, season-end reporting, and pre-planning consultations for the following year.",
    safetyAndCompliance: "All of our snow removal operations comply with WorkSafeBC regulations for winter work, including requirements for personal protective equipment, safe vehicle operation, and hazard communication. Our crews are trained in cold weather first aid, vehicle extrication procedures, and proper de-icing material handling. We carry comprehensive commercial general liability insurance with limits appropriate for Strata and commercial operations, and we are fully bonded and registered with WorkSafeBC. Our safety record reflects our commitment to protecting both our employees and the properties we serve."
