    whyChooseContent: "Renovating a condominium is a significant investment, and choosing the right contractor is the most important decision you'll make. Strata Property Services brings 35+ years of experience working specifically within Strata environments. We understand that successful condo renovation isn't just about quality craftsmanship — it's about navigating bylaws, managing logistics, respecting neighbors, and delivering predictable results. Our fixed-price quotations, dedicated project management, and comprehensive warranty program reflect our commitment to making the renovation process as smooth and stress-free as possible.",
    industryInsight: "The condominium renovation market in the Lower Mainland has grown significantly as the region's housing stock ages. Buildings constructed in the 1990s and early 2000s are now reaching the age where major component replacement is necessary — kitchens, bathrooms, flooring, and common areas all have finite lifespans. At the same time, homeowner expectations have evolved. Today's condo buyers expect modern finishes, efficient layouts, and high-quality materials. For Strata corporations, common area upgrades have become essential for maintaining property values and attracting quality purchasers. The investment in professional renovation pays dividends through increased unit values and reduced maintenance costs.",
    materialsAndMethods: "Our material selection process balances aesthetics, durability, and value. For countertops, we primarily work with quartz engineered stone from manufacturers like Caesarstone and Silestone, offering superior consistency and lower maintenance compared to natural stone. For cabinetry, our semi-custom program delivers custom-quality construction with popular door styles and finishes at 30-40% below fully custom pricing. Flooring selections include engineered hardwood, luxury vinyl plank, porcelain tile, and specialty products. We source from established distributors and can typically offer pricing below retail through our volume relationships.",
    strataSpecificContent: "Working within Strata complexes requires a different mindset than conventional residential construction. Our crews are trained in building-specific protocols: floor protection installation before any material is moved through hallways, elevator padding for material transport, daily cleanup standards that leave common areas clean and safe, noise management techniques that minimize impact on adjacent units, and respectful communication with residents, caretakers, and property managers. We carry insurance specifically endorsed for Strata renovation work, and we provide certificates of insurance directly to the Strata corporation before any work begins.",
    seasonalConsiderations: "While condo renovations can be performed year-round, certain projects benefit from seasonal timing. Exterior-related work such as window replacement or balcony waterproofing is best scheduled during dry weather months (May through September). Interior renovations can proceed in any season, though material availability and subtrade scheduling are often better during the quieter winter months (January through March). We recommend booking popular renovation services 4-8 weeks in advance, with longer lead times during the busy spring and fall seasons.",
    safetyAndCompliance: "All renovation work performed by Strata Property Services complies with the current BC Building Code, local municipal bylaws, and applicable Strata corporation regulations. Our tradespeople hold current provincial certifications in their respective disciplines, and all electrical, plumbing, and gas work is performed by licensed journeymen. We maintain comprehensive general liability insurance, course of construction coverage, and WorkSafeBC registration. Safety is integrated into every aspect of our operations — from proper scaffolding and fall protection to dust containment and hazardous material handling."
